Z||000000||Pheagey||11-11-2001||11:21 AM||||   Will the tires/rimms, rotors, calipers, radio, etc from an '87 Grand Am fit on my '88 coupe? Im getting the '87GA torrow for $300 adn hope to use it as a parts car (unless it has the quad four in it, in whick case I'll be fixing the head gasket.).<BR>   If the rotors, calipers will fit (which I hope they will) how much work and I looking at to get them on?<BR>thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||11-11-2001||11:58 AM||||Tires, rims, radio - yes.  Calipers and rotors, I'm almost positive they won't fit.  If you've got the car anyway, you can compare the parts and see how close they are, but I don'think so.  88 rotors are available from the Fiero Store for $50 each, and 88 calipers are available from most auto parts stores for around $40 front to $70 rear, plus core charge.  I believe someone in the Mall found an 88 at a pick-n-pull.  If you need to find cheap used parts, check that out.  <P>Good Luck!||||reg||14
